      "writtenOn": "2023-09-14T21:59:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "go/proto-nullness says that no for the external protobuf compiler.\n\n[And it\u0027s indeed not annotated with a non null annotation](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:out/soong/.intermediates/external/pandora/bt-test-interfaces/pandora-proto-java/android_common/xref/srcjars.xref/pandora/HostProto.java;l\u003d7209;drc\u003d57b39d9314c2fa598986453e454cb16a6df9db6d)\n\nAs we are in a test, I think I would prefer to just disable this warning, as it makes less sense in a test.\n\nFor how to do it, I guess we could put somewhere an intellij configuration that disable it for this folder or annotate the class with `@SuppressWarnings(\"ConstantConditions\")` and it seems that we will [not be the first ones to do it](https://cs.android.com/search?q\u003d%22@SuppressWarnings(%5C%22ConstantConditions%5C%22)%22\u0026sq\u003d)",
